## New in 0.07.00

* Initial Open-Source Release.

# Keep this line immediately above the last non-open-source release -- begin pe8qf1P4GCme
## New in 0.06.03

* ncp-silabs_tmsp: Fix for assert in emberProcessbinaryCommand
* wpanctl: Fix for segfault during scan when there are lots of scan results.
* Connman-plugin: Change the default node type (for joining) to router
* Various internal updates and improvements
* wpan-error: Added `kWPANTUNDStatus_NCP_Reset`.
* wpan-properties: Added `kWPANTUNDProperty_NCPRSSI` property.
* Make sure that the channel renders as a base-10 integer.
* wpan-properties: Add several thread-specific properties.
* NCPInstanceBase: Change how the IPv6 prefix is rendered. (now a string)
* ncp-silabs_tmsp: Add the lurker flag immediately if we just enabled legacy interfaces.
* ncp-silabs_tmsp: Fix for forming a network with legacy enabled.
* ncp-silabs_tmsp: Fix for joining without panid
* NCPInstanceBase: Reset NCP if the version changes after being set successfully.
* ncp-spinel: Support for OpenThread "Spinel" NCP Protocol
* Keyword scrub and boilerplate updates in preparation for open source release.
* ncp-silabs_tmsp: Fix for provisional join.

## New in 0.06.02

 *  Fix for dropped unsecured packets during legacy commissioning

## New in 0.06.01

 *  Timer: Add a check in schdedule() to ensure input interval is
    valid
 *  Major refactoring and consolidation (part 1)
 *  SetNetworkKeyTask: Change to use the proper key when commissioning
 *  ncp-silabs\_tmsp: Improvements to supporting the
    `credentials-needed` state.
 *  ncp-silabs: Fix for ConnectIP-2.0 NCP crash on join.
 *  silabs-thread-1.0: Update to support Thread-Nest-1.0.5-build-521
 *  TunnelIPv6Interface: Fix for problem where old mesh-local
    addresses stick around.
 *  socket-utils: Avoid printing out the scary (but harmless)
    `tcsetaddr() failed` error.
 *  NCPInstanceBase: Avoid complaining about the NCPDriverName
    configuration option not being supported.
 *  StatCollector: Add support for getting history for a specific node
 *  Various minor fixes and improvements
 *  Minor logging improvements

## New in 0.06.00

*  Full plug-in architecture, supporting multiple NCPs.
    *  Rename `ncp-connectip` to `ncp-silabs`.
    *  `ncp-dummy`: New dummy plugin. Does nothing.
    *  `ncp-silabs_tmsp`: New plugin for SiLabs chips using TMSP
*  Lots of refactoring and restructuring
    *  New `third_party` directory where all third party code goes
    *  Various documentation cleanups and improvements
    *  New hierarchical property names.
    *  New DBus API, NCPState, miscellaneous other improvements.
    *  headers: Move installed headers into `wpantund` subdirectory,
       instead of installing them directly into `include`
    *  New error type, `wpantund_status_t`.
*  libsoot: Alternative ASHv3 implementation for `ncp-silabs` plugin
*  wpantund: Added ability to drop privileges
*  wpantund: Added ability to chroot
*  wpantund: Adding support to send "property changed" signals over
   dbus
*  wpantund: Add support for dumping the stack after a crash
*  wpanctl: Change default node types for `join` and `form` to
   `router` and `end-device`.
*  General: Address various warnings indicated by clang and coverity
*  configure: Improve libreadline detection and behavior.
*  connman: Support for 6lowpan provision
*  StatCollector: Adding a statistics collector module in wpantund
*  Power optimization: Don't wake up the NCP if we are directly
   controlling the power of the NCP

## New in 0.05.08

* Fixed a major issue in the packet matcher which caused joining
  traffic to misbehave when there were lots of devices searching for
  an assisting device.
* Logging of TCP and UDP checksums.

## New in 0.05.07

* wpantund: Additional fix for user-added addresses after reset
* Minor logging changes
* wpan-connman-plugin: Always update the network key from NCP when we connect

## New in 0.05.06

* wpantund: Ensure user-added addresses remain usable across an NCP reset

## New in 0.05.05

* NCPControlInterface: New association state `fault`, which we now enter when bad things happen
* ncp-connectip: New property `TerminateOnFault`, which when set restores the previous behavior
* connman-plugin: Fix to enable ncp_state change to "disconnected" from "uninitialized"
* EmberNCPCtrlInterface: Changed the sleep debounce test to avoid main loop thrashing
* ncp-connectip: Fix LNA Bypass behavior
* ncp-connectip: Adjustments to firmware update process, new property `AutoUpdateFirmware`
* Coverity fixes.

## New in 0.05.04

* wpantund: Support for automatic NCP firmware upgrades
* config-file: Fixed some bugs with respect to how quoted strings were parsed.
* ncp-connectip: configure-gateway: Don't crash when the user erroneously leaves out the prefix.
* ncp-connectip: Fixed `ChannelCalGet` mfg command
* Reduced logging noise

## New in 0.05.03

* wpan-connman-plugin: Fix memory leak in plugin

## New in 0.05.02

* TunnelIPv6Interface: Fixed a NULL-pointer dereference

## New in 0.05.01

* Address various issues discovered by Coverty
* ncp-connectip: Update ActiveScan data format for Thread 1.0.2
* ncp-connectip: Added support to get the list of global IP addresses from NCP
* ncp-connectip: Only add SLAAC address when we don't already have one for a given prefix
* ncp-connectip: Various routing/addressing changes to help with being a border router
* ncp-connectip: Various ASHv3 improvements
* wpan-connman-plugin: Removed updating the IPv6 address in connman from plugin
* autoconf: Added ability to disable building of the connman plugin
* Various other minor changes and improvements

## New in 0.05.00

* Support for NCPs running SiLabs Thread 1.0 stack
* Addressed various compiler warnings that were present when building in certain environments
* conman-plugin: Various fixes and improvements
* Improved ease of building on various linux distributions
* main-loop: Added sanity checks for timeout values
* Much improved management of how IP addresses are added and removed from interfaces
* General refactoring and cleanup

## New in 0.04.04

* Renamed wpan-tunnel-driver to `wpantund`
* Backport of previous changes that were made directly to Sapphire tree.
* Fixed auto deep sleep
* Added a change to resolve the (rare) insomnia timeout issue in wpan-tunnel-driver.
* Bug fixes for connman plugin

## New in 0.04.03

* EmberNCPInstance: Fix for delay in sending management commands
* connman-plugin: Minor cleanup.
* Support for `ff03::1` multicast group on Linux
* ncp-connectip: Remove support for fetching the "Nest Token".
* Added ability to get or set the `SyslogMask` property at runtime
* connman-plugin: Improve compatibility with more recent versions of ConnMan

## New in 0.04.02

* Fixing handling of Mfg RX callback

## New in 0.04.01

* Code comment additions and changes to ignore red-herrings from coverty
* Update file boilerplate headers and refresh copyright year
* ncp-connectip: Ensured that `va_end()` is called when it should be
* ncp-connectip: Ensure continuity of commissioning connection after joining
* ncp-connectip: Remove `mWantsDeepSleepNow` member variable from `EmberNCPControlInterface`
* ncp-connectip: Only wait for `CB_LISTEN` after sleeping if NCP version has that bug

## New in 0.04.00

* Major code reorganization, refactoring, and cleanup.
  * New directory structure and file organization
  * Refactored async-I/O
  * Consolidated and organized utility functions
  * Simplified overall architecture
  * Foundation for adding support for new NCP protocols
  * Replaced most "magic numbers" with defined constants
  * Dozens of miscelaneous bug fixes and improvements
  * Cleaned up many compilation warnings
  * Renamed project `wpantund`. Executible is still named `wpan-tunnel-driver` (for now)
* Updated `man` pages for `wpanctl` and `wpan-tunnel-driver`.
* `getopt` is now used for parsing all command line arguments.
* string-utils: Properly handle interpreting the last nibble when parsing hexidecimal data blobs
* wpantund: Interface properties are now case-insensitive.
* wpantund: Support for hardware reset and explicit power-state control of NCP.
* wpantund: Lowered the amount of default logging slightly.
* wpantund: Moved property key macros to an independent header file.
* wpantund: Handle `/etc/wpantund.conf` in addition to `/etc/wpan-tunnel-driver.conf`.
* wpanctl: Now supports tab-completion, when compiled with libreadline or libedit
* wpanctl: Add channel option to scan command
* wpanctl: Fix for scan crash when there are lots of networks
* wpanctl: Support strings to name a node type
* wpanctl: Improved channel mask format for the `scan` command. (`-c 11-14,17,20-23`)
* ncp-connectip: Better, more reliable sleep behavior.
* ncp-connectip: Now supports ConnectIP-2.0.0b420, with issues.
* ncp-connectip: Fixed minor bugs with support for some SiLabs manufacturing commands.
* ncp-connectip: Added the ability to specify a ULA when joining a network.
* ncp-connectip: Fixed issue when using the default port for `PermitJoin`
* ncp-connectip: Preliminary support for separate legacy and mesh-local prefixes.
* configure: Added `--enable-ash-v3-debug` option to configure script.
* build-system: `make distclean` now works properly on systems with versions of `tar` that maxes out filenames at 99 characters.
* build-system: Clean up output of bootstrap script.
* build-system: Added pkg.m4, which contains config macros for pkg-config
* build-system: Better git integration into version reporting (specifically in tarballs made from `make dist`)
* README: Updated list of contributors.

## New in 0.03.02

* Have output from assert macros use syslog for output.
* Added `RunawayResetBackoffManager` to avoid reset loops which use 100% of CPU.

## New in 0.03.01

* Prevents bringing the interface online until we transition to a joined state.
* HostDidWake: Trigger beginning low power even when DISCONNECTED
* DBus: Fix for memory leak of get property reply messages.
* Improved support for SiLabs manufacturing commands.
* Other minor changes.

## New in 0.03.00

* Support for management protocol version 7.
* Aggressive power management for lurkers.
* Supports both ConnectIP-1.1.3 and ConnectIP-2.0.0b301
* Vastly improve how version numbers are handled and printed.
* Removed work-arounds for firmware sleep bugs.
* Now builds on a Raspberry PI.
* connman-plugin: Don't try to explicitly resume.
* Better support for interface being disabled.
* Added support for `WRITE_NEST_MAC_ADDR` command.
* Updated documentation, added `TODO.md`, `HACKING.md`.
* Added `IsAssociated` property.
* Only attempt to perform a hard reset on even failure attempts (except 0).
* Raise the default logging threshold on non-debug builds.
* EmberASHAdapter: Fix for condition which impeded throughput when loaded.
* Major refactoring and code cleanup.
* Many bug fixes.

## New in 0.02.00

* ConnectIP-2.0 support.
* Massive refactoring and cleanup.
* Improved ASH support.
* Multiple interface support.
* wpanctl: Support for retrieving multiple properties with a single call to `getprop`.
* Only send a command to the NCP after the previous command has been fully sent.
* Added file locking.
* socket-utils: Better error checking and reporting.
* Don't bring down the interface if we are in a net-wake state.
* Improved logging
* When we are in automatic deep sleep for more than 70 minutes, reset the NCP.
* Multiple interface support.
* Added many new properties.
* Fixed many, many bugs.

## New in 0.01.00

* ConnectIP-1.1 and ASHv3 support.
* Upgrade from `boost::signals` to `boost::signals2`
* Build system cleanup

## New in 0.00.06

* Fix some crashers in the ConnMan plugin.
* Fix for stripping non-ASCII characters from network names.
* Added `SetPassthruPort`, so that NCP knows what port to filter on.
* Added `any_to_bool`.
* Support for NCP sleep and enable/disable.
* Support for setting the TX power. Default is now -15dBm.
* Support for automatic failure detection.
* Updates based on feedback from https://fisheye.nestlabs.com/cru/SR-862
* NCPFirewallRule: Remove some unnecessary logging.
* connman-plugin: Make sure the lowpan device is powered at startup.
* Turn on AutoDeepSleep by default. (SAPPHIRE-6854)
* RIP table retrieval support
* CallbackStore: Fix broken `handle_all()` method.
* Use relative time instead of absolute time for various timeouts
* socket-utils: Added support for sockets to executable processes.
* Added data stream abstraction class NCPSocket.
* wpan-tunnel-driver: Added option `SyslogMask`.

## New in 0.00.05

* Support for ConnectIP-1.0.2 (support for earlier NCP versions has been dropped)
* Added NCP version check. Halts all interaction with the NCP until the version check passes.
* Robustness Improvements.
* Minor update to config script to add git commit hash to version string
* connman-plugin: Don't create a new service until we have the network key.
* connman-plugin: Stop using MTRACE, which was causing huge log files.
* connman-plugin: Fix for truncated passphrase
* Fix for: https://jira.nestlabs.com/browse/SAPPHIRE-6706
* Tickle the NCP every 60 seconds
* Miscelaneous fixes and improvements to ConnMan plugin.
* Added auto-resume property.
